Use try/finally blocks around each SSH connection usage:
```js
const local = await connectLocal();
try {
  const s1 = await start(local, LOCAL_PASS);
  console.log(...);
} finally {
  local.end();
}
```

Wrap in try/finally:
```js
const conn = await connectGcp();
try {
  await run(conn, 'systemctl restart cloudflared');
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 5_000));
  const status = await getStatus(conn);
  console.log(...);
} finally {
  conn.end();
}
```

Log or capture the JWT parse error before falling through:
```js
} catch (jwtErr) {
  // fall through to raw-base64 path; log for diagnostics
  process.stderr.write(`[debug] JWT parse failed: ${jwtErr.message}\n`);
}
```
Or at minimum use a named variable so it can be inspected during development.

Wrap the exec promise in a race against a timeout:
```js
const EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000;
const execPromise = new Promise((res, rej) => { /* existing logic */ });
const timeoutPromise = new Promise((_, rej) =>
  setTimeout(() => rej(new Error(`Command timed out after ${EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS}ms: ${cmd}`)), EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS)
);
return Promise.race([execPromise, timeoutPromise]);
```

